// P3.7 / PS21: the course's Funnel exercise (intro-to-part-studios.md PS21, `ex4-*`) through
// the UI, in inches and pounds. The numbers are asserted in `cadrs_core/tests/funnel.rs`
// (V 2.975 in³ against the course's 2.974, A 84.13 in² against 84.098, CoM (0.556, 0, −0.547),
// 0.098 lb and the inertia's Lxx 0.205, Lyy 0.518, Lxz −0.059 as `ex4-step18.png`:
// Polypropylene is 0.033 lb/in³, as Onshape's library, `ex4-step17.png`), and Sketch 1's full
// definition in `cadrs_core/tests/funnel_sketch.rs` (the sketch this scenario draws).
// PS21.7's direction: the Ø2.5 and Ø0.5 circles sit on the side away from the handle (−X), as
// the drawing shows; that is the variant whose CoM X is the screenshot's 0.556 (on +X it would
// be 0.778; the test builds both).
// 01 (PS21.1) Workspace units Inch / Pound; the document renamed "Funnel".
// 02 (PS21.2, ex4-step2) Sketch 1 on Top: the 6 × 4 ellipse, its offset 0.125 inside (the
//    rim; the 0.125 dimension between the two curves; the 6 above it and the 4 beside it), the
//    handle's three lines, a construction centreline from the origin to the end line's midpoint
//    (Coincident, Midpoint), the slanted lines Symmetric about it, the end line 1.5 long,
//    4.5 from the origin and 105° from the slanted line: fully defined (black).
// 03 (PS21.3) Extrude 1, the whole sketch, New, 0.125 in: the band and the handle.
// 04 (PS21.4, ex4-step4) Sketch 2 on the rim's bottom face (picked from the Bottom view): Use of
//    the rim's inner edge (an exact offset ellipse), offset 0.05 outwards into the rim.
// 05 (PS21.5, PS21.6, ex4-step5) the Lower Plane (Offset 3 in from Top, flipped down) and the
//    Middle Plane (Mid plane of Top and the Lower Plane), renamed in the feature list.
// 06 (PS21.7, PS21.8) Sketch 3 on the Middle Plane: Ø2.5 at x = −0.5; Sketch 4 on the Lower
//    Plane: Ø0.5 at x = −0.75.
// 07 (PS21.9, ex4-step9) Loft, Solid / Add: profiles "Faces of Sketch 2" (the disc and the 0.05
//    band, picked with the rim hidden), Sketch 3 and Sketch 4 (picked in the feature list);
//    Start and End Normal to profile, magnitudes 0.5 and 1.
// 08 (PS21.10, ex4-step10) Shell 0.05 in, the loft's top and bottom faces removed: it fails (it
//    would also shell the handle, joined to the loft): the title red with the reason, the loft
//    it shells tinted red with its edges red (P3.8: not the handle joined to it), the faces to
//    remove in the selection orange as in `ex4-step10.png`; ✓ keeps it (red in the list).
// 09 (PS21.11, ex4-step11) Loft 1 edited: the view is rolled back to it (Shell 1 isn't shown).
// 10 New: a separate part, still rolled back.
// 11 Final: the whole Part Studio as it will be, without the loft's preview: the Shell now
//    works (the thin cone). Accepted.
// 12 (PS21.12) Boolean Union, the loft first (Part 2 gives the result its properties).
// 13 (PS21.13) Fillet R0.5 on the handle's four vertical corners.
// 14 (PS21.14, ex4-step14) Sketch 5 on Front: the D-shaped bead (R0.125 arc on the handle's
//    top outer edge, closed by two vertical lines and a bottom line on the handle's bottom),
//    fully defined: the lines vertical and tangent to the arc, the bottom line level with the origin, the
//    arc's centre pierced by the handle's top outer edge; its fill over the handle translucent.
// 15 (PS21.15, X12, ex4-step15) Sweep Add, "Face of Sketch 5"; right-click → Select → Create
//    selection…, Edges, Tangent connected, the end's top edge clicked: its chain selected, 8
//    edges as Onshape's (the sliver OCCT's fillet leaves where the band's and the handle's top
//    faces meet is merged away, `brep::SLIVER`). The panel has only its ✕.
// 16 Add selection: the chain fills the Sweep path; the bead runs round the rim and handle.
// 17 (PS21.16) the spout: Extrude of the loft's bottom annulus (Bottom view), Add, 1 in down;
//    the depth arrow on the spout's end points down, the way it extrudes (fix round 1: a face
//    profile's arrow took +Z).
// 18 (PS21.17, PS21.18, ex4-step17/18) the part renamed "Funnel", Polypropylene, Mass and
//    section properties in inches and pounds. The panel reads Mass 0.098 lb, Volume 2.975 in³,
//    Surface area 84.127 in², CoM (0.556, ≈0 in scientific notation, −0.547) in, Lxx 0.205,
//    Lyy 0.518, Lxz −0.059 in² lb (the course: 0.098 lb, 2.974 in³, 84.098 in², (0.556,
//    −7.545e−5, −0.547), Lxx 0.205, Lyy 0.518, Lxz −0.059); values that would read 0.000 show
//    in scientific notation, as Onshape's.
// The fillet's corner edges are picked zoomed in, the two on the handle's far side from the
// Right and Back views (a vertical edge 0.125 in high is shorter than a vertex's pick circle);
// Sketch 2's band, under the rim, is picked with the rim hidden (shown again before 07);
// Sketches 3 and 4 in the feature list (a region click hits the first sketch plane along the
// ray).
